# HG2-A (CALLFORM, Р36 п.2): the body of f over D is `call(D; f\code)` (data first, #call-receivers); the write of y is explicit into the given data (rule Б: `data\y`), so the value reaches D as the comment says. Pins kept: seen 6, d_x 5, d_y 6. Observation: the root values are written explicitly in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract; #call-frame-20261115).
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
        int: d_x 0
        int: d_y 0
)
@: shared data[0]
# A callable launched over data it was given finds a name of its code in that data before a free input (plan M11 5a,
# the executor's reading B4): x is no place of f, D has it, and the write of y is published into D.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# The fields of D, which the dump of D showed, are the places d_x and d_y of the root.
sub: f () (int: y 0)
    data\y := x + 1
sub: main () (
    D:
        int: x 5
        int: y 0
)
    call(D; f\code)
main()
int: seen main\data\D\y
int: d_x main\data\D\x
int: d_y main\data\D\y

sub: observe ()
    shared\Observed\seen := seen
    shared\Observed\d_x := d_x
    shared\Observed\d_y := d_y
observe()
